timestamp=2026-11-09T04:50:10.848Z level=INFO run=80bcc019 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Let's parse the genealogy tree. It looks like ASCII art.\n# We need to find Dawid Majtyka's lineage and work backwards to find great-great-grandparent.\n# Also need to extract parent-child relationships from the tree structure.\n# This is a non-trivial parsing task - need to look at the actual lines carefully.\n\npath = '/app/dataset/genealogy_trees.txt'\nwith open(path) as f:\n    content = f.read()\n\n# Let's look at specific lines around \"Majtyka\" or areas that might contain it\nlines = content.splitlines()\n# Search for Majtyka\nfor i, l in enumerate(lines[:]):\n    if 'Majtyka' in l:\n        # print context\n        for j in range(max(0,i-5), min(len(lines), i+15)):\n            print(f\"{j}: {lines[j]}\")\n        break\nelse:\n    print('not found in first look')\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
