timestamp=2026-11-09T05:07:01.825Z level=INFO run=80bcc019 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Let us step back and look at the tree more directly from the top level? Or search for specific patterns.\n# Also look at how other people are connected. Maybe Juliusz Dębosz is Dawid's father, and Rozalia is his mother?\n# But Rozalia's full name is not immediately visible as \"Rozalia X\" in the same compact form. Let us look around line 85 more.\npath = '/app/dataset/genealogy_trees.txt'\nwith open(path) as f:\n    lines = f.readlines()\n\n# At line 85, we see \"Grzesiek\" at col 2973. Also above it, \"Rozalia\" appears on line 83/84? \n# And the structure shows a junction at line 79 connecting Juliusz's branch and someone else's branch to form parents of Dawid's generation?\n# Or maybe the couple is Juliusz Dębosz and Rozalia (with last name possibly Grzesiek from her line)? Or perhaps the name is \"Rozalia Grzesiek\" as a single name? \n# Or look further up from Rozalia's branch. Let us trace up from where Rozalia appears.\nl83 = lines[83]\n# find Rozalia's col\nroz_col = l83.find('Rozalia')\nprint(f'roz_col={roz_col}')\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
