timestamp=2026-11-09T05:13:18.174Z level=INFO run=80bcc019 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\npath = '/app/dataset/genealogy_trees.txt'\nwith open(path) as f:\n    lines = f.readlines()\n\n# On line 93, we see \"Kiliszek\" as a name (by itself or part of a box). Also \"Kazimierz\" is on line 92.\n# So Kazimierz is the first name, Kiliszek is the last name of the same person? \n# Look at how names are formatted elsewhere - they are written as full \"Firstname Lastname\" tokens.\n# But in this drawing, sometimes they might be split? Or maybe \"Kazimierz Kiliszek\" is the full name - let us look for the exact token as a continuous name.\n# Search for \"Kazimierz Kiliszek\" across the whole file.\nwith open(path) as f:\n    full = f.read()\nif 'Kazimierz Kiliszek' in full:\n    idx = full.find('Kazimierz Kiliszek')\n    # get line number\n    line = full[:idx].count('\\n')\n    print(line+1)\nelse:\n    print('not found')\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
