timestamp=2026-11-09T05:18:28.449Z level=INFO run=80bcc019 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\npath = '/app/dataset/genealogy_trees.txt'\nwith open(path) as f:\n    lines = f.readlines()\n\n# So no vertical connection at col 2947 above line 79. That suggests the parent of the person on Dawid's branch (as represented by that junction) might be elsewhere, or the tree is structured differently.\n# Maybe the parents are the two people whose branches merge at line 79 to form the node that produces Dawid and Kazimierz?\n# Look at what feeds into junction 2920 (left side) and 2947 (right side) from above line 79 - but we saw no vertical bar above 79 at 2947.\n# Maybe the connection is horizontal at line 79 itself? Let us look at line 79's full structure again.\nl79 = lines[79]\n# the junctions are at 2891, 2920, 2947, 2977. Between them there are horizontal connectors (-/~).\n# The shape is something like: ---+---+---+---  with branches going down at some + and up at others?\n# Branches going down have | below? Or the other way. Branches going up to parents have | above the junction? Or the junction connects to parent above via the line.\n# But we didn't see | above at 2947. Let us look at the entire column range above 79 more broadly.\nj = 2947\n# look at line 78-70 for any non-space char within 5 cols of j\nfor i in range(78, 65, -1):\n    l = lines[i]\n    # scan window\n    for k in range(j-3, j+4):\n        if k >= 0 and k < len(l):\n            if l[k] != ' ':\n                print(f\"{i},{k}: {l[k]}\")\n    # if found something, break\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
