timestamp=2026-11-09T05:19:21.186Z level=INFO run=80bcc019 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# The tree is very complex ASCII. Let us look at the full file in raw form but search differently.\n# Maybe use python to actually parse the tree structure properly. Let us write a simple parser that tracks lines and columns.\n# Another common format: the tree uses |, +, -, ~ to connect. Names appear at nodes. Let us build a graph by connecting children to parents based on vertical positioning.\npath = '/app/dataset/genealogy_trees.txt'\nwith open(path) as f:\n    lines = f.readlines()\n\n# Build a list of all names with their positions (row, col)\nimport re\nnodes = []\nfor i, l in enumerate(lines):\n    # match names\n    for m in re.finditer(r'\\b([A-Z][a-ząęćłńóśźż]{2,}(?:\\s+[A-Z][a-ząęćłńóśźż]{2,})+)\\b', l):\n        name = m.group(1)\n        nodes.append((i, m.start(), name))\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
