timestamp=2026-11-09T05:45:10.309Z level=INFO run=80bcc019 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Maybe the tree structure is simpler than it looks. Let us look at the first few lines differently - maybe the tree is organized in a hierarchical way.\n# Or let us look at all names in order from top to bottom and try to understand generations.\npath = '/app/dataset/genealogy_trees.txt'\nwith open(path) as f:\n    lines = f.readlines()\n\n# Get all names with their row numbers, sorted by row\nimport re\nall_names = []\nfor i, l in enumerate(lines):\n    for m in re.finditer(r'\\b([A-Z][a-ząęćłńóśźż]{2,}\\s+[A-Z][a-ząęćłńóśźż]{2,})\\b', l):\n        all_names.append((i+1, m.group(1)))\n\n# Group by approximate row ranges (generations)\nall_names.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])\n# Show first 30\nfor n in all_names[:30]:\n    print(n)\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
