timestamp=2026-11-09T05:50:04.302Z level=INFO run=80bcc019 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Not much at the top. Let us look further down from the beginning. Also look at the bottom? Or look at the overall shape.\n# Another approach - let us load the people accounts and also look at the tree file completely as-is, then try to reconstruct by tracing all vertical connections systematically.\n# This is a bit ambiguous from the drawing. Let us look at a different part of the tree - maybe the \"Banak\" or other names that appear at edges? Also look for \"Żakiewicz\" etc.\npath = '/app/dataset/genealogy_trees.txt'\nwith open(path) as f:\n    lines = f.readlines()\n\n# Look for 'Adam Gałach' specifically if it exists as full name\nfor i, l in enumerate(lines):\n    if 'Adam Gałach' in l:\n        print(f'FOUND at {i+1}')\n        break\nelse:\n    # look for Adam and Gałach close\n    for i, l in enumerate(lines):\n        if 'Adam' in l and 'Gałach' in l:\n            print(f'{i+1}: {l}', end='')\n            break\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
